Absent: [kmain] shutting down

Intermediate failures retained:
1. A concurrent ext4 cache edit initially failed compilation on missing bool and const-discard errors; later corrected. EXIT=2.
2. The first shared writable-drive run failed with Failed to get write lock. EXIT=2. Drive flags were then scoped to the default system image, made read-only, and old BOOT_MODULES entries no longer carry a drive.
3. make check failed in the ext4 standalone demo because a failed mount left fs.image non-NULL. The implementation was fixed to clear mount state on failure; no assertion was removed.
4. The legacy unsupported-depth vector used eh_depth=1, which became supported under M5 and was malformed as an index tree. The vector was changed to eh_depth=2 while preserving the original EXT4_UNSUPPORTED assertion.
5. Early virtio revisions timed out before idle or failed ext4 mount. Fixes included legacy GuestPageSize/QueueAlign/QueuePFN, contiguous queue frames, modern queue register offsets, feature negotiation, and a bounded completion timeout. The final run above reaches idle and also reads /motd successfully.

Boundary: this log completes M1 only. The integrated storage lines are M5 progress and do not prove U-mode IPC storage, interrupt-driven completion, a pager, or a shell.